{"id": "EUVD-2026-103911", "enisaUuid": "e393b288-47c5-378c-a9ee-a2074a0e9480", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: proximity: pulsedlight: fix iio_device left registered on PM setup failure\n\npm_runtime_set_active() failing in probe() jumps to error_unreg_buffer,\nwhich only calls iio_triggered_buffer_cleanup() -- it does not undo the\niio_device_register() that already succeeded a few lines above. probe()\nthen returns the error, the devm-managed indio_dev is freed, but the\niio core still has it registered: the sysfs/chardev nodes stay live and\npoint at freed memory.\n\nAdd an error_unreg_dev label that unregisters the iio device before\nfalling through to the existing buffer cleanup, mirroring the teardown\norder already used in lidar_remove().", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:44:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c8211eef98929c5188f8c2224e83b9a63b41bd1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06fa13c53442257b94ea1519555ceddaaea57e0d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/20ebd7f4e35c0a737f011bc83aeb0cdd37507648", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e462b47b9637b8c0285f4a38b5af9a322847d164", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4daa9ca557b4b98ae1ad38a6d1deaa3e31eb8edf"], "aliases": ["GHSA-26f7-hh7p-wmqm", "CVE-2026-98657"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "21c8a9fe-4c48-3ad3-b788-248faee67241", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4ac4e086fd8c59e6b69089e6f7605500b63a6d17 <20ebd7f4e35c0a737f011bc83aeb0cdd37507648"}, {"id": "267dc2a5-c301-3063-bfe6-208c002cecbd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4ac4e086fd8c59e6b69089e6f7605500b63a6d17 <06fa13c53442257b94ea1519555ceddaaea57e0d"}, {"id": "4b9d56e6-9e0f-37d4-b00a-fc8d51893c30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "4edf31fa-2414-356e-9439-aa8c8e45b3ca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "51163ddd-c00a-3001-8702-bf51a09017a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5d18fd65-6d32-3131-a5e2-35ce33a165dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "61ab182c-0321-3b3a-bc28-720f810d8194", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4ac4e086fd8c59e6b69089e6f7605500b63a6d17 <2c8211eef98929c5188f8c2224e83b9a63b41bd1"}, {"id": "6ebe85ae-1ab8-3fc2-b552-7f35d255d935", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4ac4e086fd8c59e6b69089e6f7605500b63a6d17 <e462b47b9637b8c0285f4a38b5af9a322847d164"}, {"id": "890db354-02b6-3a84-b1bd-f55c55e3cfb8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "8c19648b-5899-3ca4-9693-3a84694d422e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "bd91d759-1b3d-3876-afe2-35e759c8d95c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.5"}, {"id": "d3d6d890-0a6b-3c00-8bd2-86213323c50e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4ac4e086fd8c59e6b69089e6f7605500b63a6d17 <4daa9ca557b4b98ae1ad38a6d1deaa3e31eb8edf"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "294d783a-628c-3432-bd0a-0ba3be056ba7", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}